RISC-V: give a saturating conversion to a small type a temporary register of its own.

genIntrinsic writes the result register of NI_PRIMITIVE_SaturateTo(U)Int8/16 and then loads the bounds
into the temporary register. LSRA could give both the same register when the operand stays live after
the conversion; the temporary register is now delay-free.

Regression test: bflat-ts:softfloat/soft_float_conv

diff --git a/src/coreclr/jit/lsrariscv64.cpp b/src/coreclr/jit/lsrariscv64.cpp
--- a/src/coreclr/jit/lsrariscv64.cpp
+++ b/src/coreclr/jit/lsrariscv64.cpp
@@ -457,7 +457,9 @@ int LinearScan::BuildNode(GenTree* tree)
                     assert(op2 == nullptr);
                     assert(op1->TypeIs(TYP_INT));
                     assert(tree->TypeIs(TYP_INT));
+                    // The bound is loaded after the result register is written, so they must differ.
                     buildInternalIntRegisterDefForNode(tree);
+                    setInternalRegsDelayFree = true;
                     break;
 
                 default:
